{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Eloise >:3c","id":"260820438026813440","is_bot":0,"username":"effervescenteloise"},"author_id":"260820438026813440","channel_id":"852742259073744937","content":"The bark of Cael’fii begins to wither thanks to the shards of cold iron, but after a few moments, the wooden gunsmith exclaims and clambers up the sheer surface of Cael’fii on all fours, moving far more fluidly than seems possible. They reach the crown of the tree and whisper a short series of words in sylvan that sound like half-request, half-prayer. They press the device up against the trunk and it melds into the surface of the bark as though being dropped into oil. There is a thunderous shake before a bright burst of purple-green light radiates out from the gentle mother. For a moment, the entire burrough is shrouded in a calm light that can be seen throughout the city. Then there is a snapping sound and a large rush of wind as simultaneously, all pure iron in the burrough is transformed into a composite or another metal entirely (the function of player tools and weapons will not be affected). At first the redcoats seem confused, before the fey denizens of the burrough swarm over them. They are getting hurt and burned, but they are able to fight much better. Within a matter of minutes the redcoats are driven back, suffering heavy losses. Ferrytown is safe.\n\nHowever, as the purple light dissipates it passes over the other burroughs, affecting their metals to some extent as well. What implications this may have for Empire CIty is as of yet unknown.","created_at":"2021-07-31T07:08:59.613000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"870926000798695445","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
